# NOTE (multi-arch readiness): the bochs/qxl/vmwgfx/vboxvideo modules
# here are specific to x86 virtual machines. Since initramfs-tools
# silently skips a module that does not exist, this file is harmless on
# arm64 as well; virtio_gpu and simpledrm apply there too.
# Kavis — kernel modules forced into the initramfs
#
# WHY: Plymouth draws the boot screen on the DRM (KMS) device. If the
# driver is not in the initramfs there is no DRM device either; Plymouth
# falls back to text mode and kernel/systemd text scrolls instead of the
# splash. initramfs-tools' "most" list takes storage and file system
# drivers, it does not guarantee display drivers.
#
# The ones below are virtual machine display adapters. Real hardware
# drivers (i915, amdgpu, nouveau) already come with "most"; these are for
# environments like QEMU/VirtualBox/VMware. An unknown module name
# produces a warning, it does not stop the build.

# QEMU stdvga — "bochs" on kernel 6.x, "bochs_drm" before
bochs
bochs_drm
# QEMU -vga qxl
qxl
# QEMU -vga virtio and virtio-gpu
virtio_gpu
# VMware / VirtualBox
vmwgfx
vboxvideo
# The generic DRM device the kernel sets up when there is no vendor driver
simpledrm

# --- Real hardware display drivers -------------------------------------
# Plymouth's FRAMEBUFFER=y hook already takes these with "most", but that
# behaviour depends on initramfs-tools' internal list; writing them
# explicitly here guarantees it and lets the 0300-plymouth hook verify
# their presence. If the splash starts late, look here first: if the
# driver is not in the initramfs the DRM device does not appear until the
# root is mounted.
# (there is no i915 on arm64; initramfs-tools skips an unknown module
# with a warning, it does not produce an error.)
i915
amdgpu
nouveau

# --- Sound cards ------------------------------------------------------
# WHY: the boot music can only play once /dev/snd/pcm* appears. If the
# sound module loads after the root file system is mounted, the music
# starts in the MIDDLE of the boot screen (a few seconds of delay were
# seen in the VirtualBox test). With the modules in the initramfs the
# device is ready much earlier and the music starts together with the
# splash.
# QEMU/VirtualBox Intel HD Audio
snd_hda_intel
snd_hda_codec_generic
# VirtualBox ICH AC97 (old default)
snd_intel8x0
snd_ac97_codec
# virtio sound (QEMU)
virtio_snd
